 of Saul","p":"may-rawb'","t":"merab","g":"Merab","fb":[["merab","Merab","Woman living at the time of United Monarchy","The elder of Saul's two daughters. Saul promised her to David after Goliath and then gave her to Adriel of Meholah instead. Her five sons by Adriel were later handed over to the Gibeonites and executed for Saul's slaughter of their people.","person",3]],"v":[7557,7693,7695]},"H4780":{"l":"מַרְדּוּת","x":"mardûwth","d":"rebelliousness","p":"mar-dooth'","t":"marduth","g":"rebelliousness","fb":[],"v":[7760]},"H4770":{"l":"מַרְבֵּק","x":"marbêq","d":"a stall (for cattle)","p":"mar-bake'","t":"marbeq","g":"of [the] stall","fb":[],"v":[7966,20065,22453,23139]},"H4794":{"l":"מְרוּצָה","x":"mᵉrûwtsâh","d":"a race (the act), whether the manner or the progress","p":"mer-oo-tsaw'","t":"merutsah","g":"the running","fb":[],"v":[8505,8505,19158,19493]},"H4739":{"l":"מָקַץ","x":"Mâqats","d":"Makats, a place in Palestine","p":"maw-kats'","t":"maqats","g":"Makaz","fb":[["makaz","Makaz","","Solomon had twelve officers feeding his household, and Ben-deker's district took in Makaz, Shaalbim and Beth-shemesh. That one verse is all there is, and the site has never been found.","place",1]],"v":[8853]},"H4734":{"l":"מִקְלַעַת","x":"miqlaʻath","d":"a sculpture (probably in bas-relief)","p":"mik-lah'-ath","t":"miqlaath","g":"carvings","fb":[],"v":[8914,8925,8928,8965]},"H4778":{"l":"מֶרֶד","x":"Mered","d":"Mered, an Israelite","p":"meh'-red","t":"mered","g":"Mered","fb":[["mered","Mered","Man living at the time of Divided Monarchy","A man of Judah who married Bithiah, a daughter of Pharaoh, as well as a wife called \"the Jewess.\" Towns and craftsmen were counted among his descendants in the genealogies of Chronicles.","person",2]],"v":[10402,10403]},"H4732":{"l":"מִקְלוֹת","x":"Miqlôwth","d":"Mikloth, a place in the Desert","p":"mik-lohth'","t":"miqloth","g":"Mikloth","fb":[["mikloth","Mikloth","Man living at the time of United Monarchy","A man of the Benjamite family that