"d":"properly, to soften by rubbing or pressure; hence (medicinally) to apply as an emollient","p":"maw-rakh'","t":"marach","g":"let them rub [it]","fb":[],"v":[18410]},"H4757":{"l":"מְרֹאדַךְ בַּלְאָדָן","x":"Mᵉrôʼdak Balʼâdân","d":"Merodak-Baladan, a Babylonian king","p":"mer-o-dak' bal-awdawn'","t":"merodak baladan","g":"Merodach-Baladan","fb":[["merodach-baladan","Merodach-baladan","King living at the time of Divided Monarchy","A Chaldean chief who seized Babylon's throne and fought Assyria in the late eighth century BC. He sent envoys to Hezekiah when the king got well, probably looking for an ally, and Hezekiah showed them everything in his treasury, which brought Isaiah's warning of exile to Babylon. Assyrian records of Sargon II and Sennacherib know him as Marduk-apla-iddina II.","person",1]],"v":[18412,18412]},"H4752":{"l":"מַר","x":"mar","d":"a drop","p":"mar","t":"mar","g":"a drop","fb":[],"v":[18434]},"H4741":{"l":"מַקְצֻעָה","x":"maqtsuʻâh","d":"a scraper, i.e. a carving chisel","p":"mak-tsoo-aw'","t":"maqtsuah","g":"tools","fb":[],"v":[18545]},"H4718":{"l":"מַקֶּבֶת","x":"maqqebeth","d":"properly, a perforator, i.e. a hammer (as piercing); also (intransitively) a perforation, i.e. a quarry","p":"mak-keh'-beth","t":"maqqebeth","g":"[the] excavation","fb":[],"v":[18673]},"H4788":{"l":"מָרוּד","x":"mârûwd","d":"an outcast; (abstractly) destitution","p":"maw-rood'","t":"marud","g":"homeless people","fb":[],"v":[18792,20316,20372]},"H4711":{"l":"מָצַץ","x":"mâtsats","d":"to suck","p":"maw-tsats'","t":"matsats","g":"you may suck","fb":[],"v":[18932]},"H4771":{"l":"מַרְגּוֹעַ","x":"margôwaʻ","d":"a resting place","p":"mar-go'-ah","t":"margoa","g":"rest","fb":[],"v":[19104]},"H4798":{"l":"מַרְזֵחַ","x":"marzêach","d":"a cry, i.e. (of grief) a lamentation","p":"mar-zay'-akh","t":"marzeach","g":"[the] revelry","fb":[],"v":[19340,22456]},"H4781":{"l":"מְרֹדָךְ","x":"Mᵉrôdâk","d":"Merodak, a Babylonian idol","p":"mer-o-dawk'","t":"merodak","g":"Marduk","fb":[["merodach","Merodach","A male deity in the Old Testament","Marduk, Babylon's chief god. Jeremiah announces Babylon's fall with \"Merodach is broken in pieces.\" The Cyrus Cylinder credits Marduk with handing Babylon to Cyrus, the very fall the oracle looks for.","person",1]],"v":[20167]},"H4738":{"l":"מִקְסָם","x":"miqçâm","d":"an augury","p":"mik-sawn'","t":"miqcam","g":"divination","fb":[],"v":[20703,20714]},"H4767":{"l":"מִרְבָּה","x":"mirbâh","d":"abundance, i.e. a great quantity","p":"meer-baw'","t":"mirbah","g":"much","fb":[],"v":[21038]},"H4769":{"l":"מַרְבֵּץ","x":"marbêts","d":"a reclining place, i.e. fold (for flocks)","p":"mar-bates'","t":"marbets","g":"a resting place","fb":[],"v":[21087,22819]},"H4756":{"l":"מָרֵא","x":"mârêʼ","d":"a master","p":"maw-ray'","t":"mare","g":"lord","fb":[],"v":[21804,21855,21860,21896]},"H4710":{"l":"מִצְפֻּן","x":"mitspun","d":"a secret (place or thing, perhaps, treasure)","p":"mits-poon'","t":"mitspun","g":"treasures","fb":[],"v":[22515]},"H4796":{"l":"מָרוֹת","x":"Mârôwth","d":"Maroth, a place in Palestine","p":"maw-rohth'","t":"maroth","g":"of Maroth","fb":[["maroth","Maroth","","Micah names it in his lament over the towns of the Judean lowlands as Assyria came, playing its name against the Hebrew for \"bitterness.\" Nobody knows where it was, only that it sat in the same district as Lachish and Moresheth.","place",1]],"v":[22590]}}